DEFINE SYSTEM order-platform
DESCRIPTION Takes orders from the storefront, charges the customer, and hands fulfilment to the warehouse

DEFINE COMPONENT storefront
DESCRIPTION The customer-facing web application that builds a cart and submits an order
ALWAYS submit orders through the order-service API
NEVER read from the orders database directly

DEFINE COMPONENT order-service
DESCRIPTION Owns the order lifecycle: created, paid, fulfilled, cancelled
ALWAYS validate an order before charging it
WHEN an order is paid THEN publish an order-paid event
NEVER call the payment-provider directly
WHEN a card is declined THEN call the payment-provider to retry once

DEFINE COMPONENT payment-service
DESCRIPTION The only component that talks to the external payment-provider
ALWAYS record every charge attempt with its outcome
WHEN a charge succeeds THEN notify order-service

DEFINE COMPONENT warehouse-adapter
ALWAYS consume order-paid events
WHEN an order-paid event arrives THEN create a pick list
NEVER change an order's state

ASSERT storefront depends only on order-service
ASSERT order-service publishes order-paid exactly once per order
ASSERT inventory-service reserves stock before an order is paid
ASSERT payment-service is the only caller of payment-provider
